# Pull Requests — Creating GitHub PRs (UI + `gh`)

Created: 2026-02-02 05:40 UTC  
Last reviewed: 2026-02-02 05:44 UTC

This is a practical guide to opening PRs in GitHub with good defaults.

## Before You Open the PR
- Ensure branch is pushed:
```sh
git push -u origin HEAD
```
- Confirm the diff is what you expect:
```sh
git diff origin/main...HEAD
```

## Create a PR in the GitHub UI
1) Push your branch.
2) Open the repo on GitHub → “Compare & pull request”.
3) Fill title/body (use `architecture/2-knowledge-base/pull-requests/pr-body-template.mdc`).
4) Add:
   - reviewers
   - labels
   - linked issue (if applicable)
5) If it’s not ready for review, create as **Draft**.

## Create a PR with `gh`
```sh
gh pr create --fill
```

Common options:
```sh
gh pr create --draft --fill
gh pr create --title "Fix checkout spinner on API error" --body-file - < pr-body.md
gh pr view --web
```

## Link Issues
Use auto-closing keywords when appropriate:
- “Fixes #123”
- “Closes #123”

If you don’t want auto-close, just link the issue URL.

## After Opening
- Watch CI and link results in the PR if CI isn’t automatically visible.
- If you pushed follow-up commits, keep the PR updated with a short summary.
